{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how","id":1332015,"title":"Do you use memories of previous Exaltations in your chronicles? How?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-21T14:01:50-07:00","id":1332015,"title":"Do you use memories of previous Exaltations in your chronicles? How?","content":"I tried using it a bit in my old game to give backstory to why an NPC was an enemy (a Sidereal) but it didn't work that well. No one was really invested in such a non-organic villain.<br /> <br /> In my previous 3rd ed game, I used it to write a little bit of fiction just to fill out the world (and because I enjoyed writing short fiction). So I've mostly been doing kept doing that for 3rd ed Lunars; the PCs have dreams sometimes at night, of the interactions between different PCs' previous incarnations. Sometimes I send them all the same thing, sometimes they get slightly different ones.<br /> <br /> This is mostly just to fill out the world, and do a little foreshadowing for later in the game. I write about two pages per three sessions I guess. Just short sections, a few paragraphs, to show a dream/memory of a scene. It's not really about making the previous incarnations a big thing (none are named, and it's not like it's the same ones again and again; they do have 6500 years of previous incarnations after all).<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing I found in my previous game (a high-xp Solar-Lunar game) is that, essentially, some people were quite interested in their previous incarnations, but most weren't. That might just be my group; perhaps other groups are a bit different. So generally stuff related to their previous incarnations doesn't grab them that much (a couple were, as I said). So I'm wondering whether other STs have used previous incarnations a lot, what you found worked and didn't work, what you do currently, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-21-2019, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:14:39-07:00","id":1332018,"title":"","content":"I tried 'story time' in a non-Exalted campaign once, and it fizzled. The idea was to give the campaign some color and eventually to work a few of the old legends in, but it became chat time for the players, so I stopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:19:51-07:00","id":1332021,"title":"","content":"I wrote flashbacks for players from their past lives in the first Exalted game I ever ran for my local group, and my playergroup took that as the default mode for the gameline. Now they all include them in every game they run. It's pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:25:58-07:00","id":1332023,"title":"","content":"I've used them as a storyline in a DB game before specifically as an attempt to fill out the world and expand on its backstory. Most players enjoyed it but one didn't. And as a player, I often find myself relatively uninterested in exploring that sort of past; often my characters have enough problems without needing to add another one to it.<br /> <br /> I think it depends heavily on your players on how you want to do it; I don't think it's a bad thing all the time but it does require some buy in. In one game I'm in one of the players cares a lot about his prior incarnation to the point of it being a main antagonist in the game as a Deathlord, while a different player killed his PC specifically because he wanted to play as their Reincarnation and explore that aspect, while I'm not particularly interested in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:27:03-07:00","id":1332024,"title":"","content":"My Lore Supernal had an RP thing where whenever he would enter bonfire anima he would become possessed by his very first Incarnation, who would take over his body while he lost consciousness. This lead to interesting dynamics as the first Incarnation knew things the current one did not and vice versa, and neither could talk directly to the other.<br /> <br /> Also the first Incarnation was much more wise and mature, which enraged my character to no end because he was (and still is) convinced that he is the greatest mind to ever live. This was reflected in mechanics too - only the first Incarnation could use certain Lore Charms, because the current Incarnation lacked the humility necessary to master them.<br /> <br /> After much drama and a little bit of growing up, the Lore Supernal &quot;made peace&quot; with his first Incarnation and accepted it into himself, ascending to Essence 3 and unlocking his full potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:58:32-07:00","id":1332028,"title":"","content":"Before each session I usually try to write out a couple of pages as a short story that people can read before we play. These stories will flesh out the world in some way. For example, they might show what's going on with important NPC's in the setting, or show how parts of the setting where the PCs are not currently located are changing. I will also sometimes write these as flashback memories for a couple of characters if they are going somewhere or doing something for which having a past connection to a place or an individual is important.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I will also sometimes have a descriptive moment for PC's when they encounter the ruins of a First Age building or device. The player might momentarily have a flash where they remember the crumbling structure in all of its glory or see the older structure briefly superimposed over the ruins. This can help to highlight the sense of &quot;loss&quot; and the idea that the world has fallen from where it used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T15:24:59-07:00","id":1332029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1332023#post1332023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In one game I'm in one of the players cares a lot about his prior incarnation to the point of it being a main antagonist in the game as a Deathlord,</div> </div> </div> </div>I made this the centrepiece of part of my plot in 2nd ed. The party decided to go fight Walker in Darkness (not something I pushed them towards, they just decided by themselves), and so I decided that I'chan, the Twilight, would be the reincarnation of Ozandus Pal - ie Walker in Darkness. They'd go to the Invisible Fortress, find the Forgotten Blade, and discover Walker in Darkness's past, which they could then use to defeat him.<br /> Then another PC accidentally killed I'chan in a fight against some Sidereals while they were limit breaking, and the plot kind of fell apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while a different player killed his PC specifically because he wanted to play as their Reincarnation and explore that aspect, while I'm not particularly interested in it. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'd kill off a PC to do so, but I actually like this; I played 2 (or 3? I forget) Zeniths in a row that were reincarnations, in some ways very similar characters and in others very different.<br /> <br /> I'd also quite like to play the reincarnation of my Night caste who died about 10 sessions ago, but I don't really have any good concepts for a Night that I want to play.<br /> Actually, that Night was the reincarnation of a Night my friend played in 2nd ed (I asked him for permission), who got killed in the second-to-last fight of the campaign (by 3 Abyssals in a room deep beneath the Imperial Manse). That guy himself was a reincarnation of a previous Night that guy had played.<br /> <br /> I generally like people to play their own reincarnations; if the character seems to be roleplayed similarly to the previous character, well, that's why.<br /> In reality however, it's generally not practical; if you're up to Essence 3, it might seem odd for some girl to get exalted a week ago (a week after the previous character died) to have as much experience as everyone else. And more to the point, it's generally not the case that if a Zenith dies, the next character to turn up is a Zenith.<br /> <br /> Recently, for example, a Changing Moon in my Lunars game died. The player then brought in a Full Moon. I'd have liked to say he was the new incarnation, but honestly, it wouldn't fit his backstory (or Caste) to have been exalted three days ago.<br /> <br /> And of course, it means you can keep using the same First-Age remnant plot if you're doing something like that (for example, if the PCs found an ancient temple dedicated to their old Circle, you don't have to retcon who was in that circle).<br /> <br /> And this isn't something any of my playgroup have expressed interest in, I think it's just me.<br /> <br /> Still, the next time one dies and is replaced (probably months later in-game, at least) I can hopefully say it's the new incarnation of the Changing Moon who died. None of my players care much about this, but I find it satisfying, and if it doesn't get in the way of their concept they're generally fine with me declaring this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> This is a slight tangent from the main question of the thread, but I think it's an interesting one. I'd be interested to hear what other people do with this, if anyone else likes to play or see played the reincarnations of previous PCs.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T15:28:21-07:00","id":1332030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1332028#post1332028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before each session I usually try to write out a couple of pages as a short story that people can read before we play. These stories will flesh out the world in some way. For example, they might show what's going on with important NPC's in the setting, or show how parts of the setting where the PCs are not currently located are changing. I will also sometimes write these as flashback memories for a couple of characters if they are going somewhere or doing something for which having a past connection to a place or an individual is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is somewhat similar to me, though tbh I do it even if there is no important connection.<br /> <br /> I've sent the PCs like, 3 or 4 pages of First Age memories now (not in one go, over six sessions), but after a while that might get dry. Fleshing out the world seems like a good idea. I don't really like doing things like &quot;what's going on with important NPCs&quot; because the PCs shouldn't know (I did do it for some NPCs after the end of my 2nd ed game, but it was the end so that didn't matter). But I think maybe just really ordinary people who are tangentially affected by the PCs will flesh out the world well, remind them of the local cultures, mores, details they should have noticed but didn't, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T16:12:25-07:00","id":1332037,"title":"","content":"Most of the previous-incarnation-memories scenes I\u2019ve done have either been momentary flashes when they encounter some other Celestial Exalt, a city that was around in the First Age, or an artifact that was personal to a previous incarnation of theirs; or it\u2019s been part of a dream sequence. <br /> <br /> Dreams played a big part in my seafaring game, as one of the prominent NPCs was the goddess of Exalted dreams, who ran a parlor in Chiaroscuro where one could pay to have hand-tailored dreams made by her underlings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T19:53:39-07:00","id":1332057,"title":"","content":"I think in the past five years I've only used it once, and it was when my players were investigating a ghost ship. Like a ship that had sunk and was full of ghosts, and the battle only went so far as the eclipse flaring his anima banner, at which point all the maligned spirits in the place took a knee and obeyed their returned captain. I didn't ask permission from the player, but he enjoyed it and I think it worked well. Overall though I find most of my players have thoughts along the lines of &quot;That was literally ages past, and we don't want to repeat the mistakes of the first age anyway so who cares?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T08:18:12-07:00","id":1332132,"title":"","content":"Have used considerably as a tool of world-building and way too add plots hooks - truth be told even more as a player than ST, might be said.<br /> Usually pays off in the insertion of major NPCs, be they allies, mentors or antagonists (sometimes two or more combined) plotlines and such.<br /> <br /> In fact most of the time i leave it vague and only start to mess with my own PC's past lives after 2-3 sessions of the game, as my way introduce stuff that interests but i feel may be somewhat missing at that stage or twisting certain types of narratives.<br /> <br /> For example, while a number of my character have had Lunar lovers, half the time they were <b><i>not </i></b>their &quot;mates&quot;, resulting in romantic triangles or polygons of varied levels of tidiness/messiness among other things. One particular game involved me &amp; another PC as the (both female) reincarnations of Amyana, Arkadi and a very, very besieged Leviathan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A more serious one was the decision to make a previous incarnation of my 3e Twilight, while quite long lived &amp; badass in its own way (ruler of an empire shaped in the Wyld, with a number of lieutenants/pupils/viziers under him), wholly a product of the Age of Sorrows, as a way to break out of a &quot;everything high level/badass happened in the First Age, maybe Shogunate&quot; 2e influenced tendency i saw in my group. While quite dead indeed and producing no Deathlord (in fact his death is related to backing off at the last moment from turning into a super-abyssal, so to speak), his heirs/generals/sucessors and his empire with an empty throne have been quite the mine of plots for the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall involving the players in the process is a major part - try fo get some bits from them on the subject beforehand. Not exactly previous incarnations per se, but past eras, strange places, objects &amp; beings, some peculiar combo, riff or twist on the current PC's capacities. The point with them is to see what catches their interest or not - and how can it relate to the current incarnations of the characters and play. Vignettes are nice, but <b>interactivity </b>is of the essence for them to roleplay with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-01-2019, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T08:41:23-07:00","id":1332134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1332037#post1332037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreams played a big part in my seafaring game, as one of the prominent NPCs was the goddess of Exalted dreams, who ran a parlor in Chiaroscuro where one could pay to have hand-tailored dreams made by her underlings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably these were dreams of all kinds then; previous incarnations, prophecies, symbolic metaphors, bizzare mash-ups of what the PCs had been thinking of, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T08:43:58-07:00","id":1332135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1332132#post1332132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, while a number of my character have had Lunar lovers, half the time they were <b><i>not </i></b>their &quot;mates&quot;, resulting in romantic triangles or polygons of varied levels of tidiness/messiness among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of our Lunars married one of the Solars... who's not her destined mate, but he just assumed she was, and she's been paranoid that at some point his real Mate would turn up and try and steal him.<br /> No-one realises that actually her (adopted) father, the other Lunar, is actually her mate. He doesn't even realise, because he's been told the Bond is a romantic thing, and clearly his daughter and son-in-law are Bonded, he just loves the Night Caste like a son because, well, it's his son-in-law.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T10:12:07-07:00","id":1332144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1332134#post1332134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably these were dreams of all kinds then; previous incarnations, prophecies, symbolic metaphors, bizzare mash-ups of what the PCs had been thinking of, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The goddess would have her dream flies gather information while they were out doing their regular duties. Any time they encountered an Exalt, the little gods would shadow them for a bit, learn the kind of stuff they were interested in, and assemble a profile about the Exalt in question. Following that, she would have her dream flies appear to said Exalt and offer up tailored dreams, often related to something they were aspiring towards. In exchange, they were asked to foster worship for her and build occasional shrines.<br /> <br /> Since Seamstress was interested in an amulet that housed the torpid soul of a Deathlord, the goddess sent her dream flies out to find it, and when they did, they made episodic dreams for her in which she experienced the life of the man who held it at the time.<br /> <br /> \u200bSince Barbus wanted the Crown of Thunders for his tribe, the goddess had her dream flies cobble together a vision of the Usurpation in which he (as Marela) threw the crown into the sea to stop the traitorous Dragon-Blooded from taking it off her corpse. (And no, he wasn't the reincarnation of Marela, but she didn't tell him that.)<br /> <br /> \u200bSince Gasp of the Drowning murdered the dream flies sent to gather information about him, she stopped sending them his way.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T18:41:49-07:00","id":1332212,"title":"","content":"For our current Chronicle, The Storm This Way Comes, I've been turning the usual Exalted tropes around and upside down as much as I can. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Instead of past lives, we're exploring future lives. So far, my players have figured out that they encountered something like a &quot;save point&quot; and that for whatever reason, they got bounced back 7 years to do things over.<br /> <br /> Each of the Celestials has a parallel present + future. The time effect wasn't perfect everywhere, so they're finding evidence left behind. Not everyone was in the same Circle the first time through. Everyone had a different path.... some happier and some tragic. Some found their true loves, and some became bitter, mercenary, and alone. And some didn't survive the whole span. <br /> <br /> I'm borrowing an idea from B5, and using a question as a fundamental feature of the story: If you could do things over again, what would you do differently?<br /> <br /> We also do have some effects of past lives, but I'm trying to minimize them. Basically just enough for Lunar or Solar mates to show up, or to be a backstory to detail up.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T23:04:27-07:00","id":1332234,"title":"","content":"Very interesting! I'm trying to do things differently and bring in some twists with my own game (as we've playing Exalted almost weekly for 12 years, so even with the new edition it's a little stale); that's a good idea, I might do something a little similar. I don't think they would expect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T04:02:48-07:00","id":1332262,"title":"","content":"The odd thing about &quot;past lives&quot; is that it's either personal (and we care) or not (and we don't). <hr /><br /> <b>It's useful if you get players to do brief blurbs on their past lives.</b> Treating past lives as variants on my current character, I could highlight consistent themes or ideas for my concept - and anything the changes is clearly superficial. As an ST, you might see:<ul><li>&quot;Oh, this Eclipse always favors Occult - she's a shaman or diplomat for spirits. But her region/culture varies and influences her little since she seems to always abandon them in favor of her work as a messenger and spiritualist.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">.</span></li> <li>&quot;Oh, this Dawn has a multi-incarnation rivalry against Isidoros. Perhaps he rather stories about fighting demons or giant beasts - instead of leading armies against the Realm. Less Wyld Hunts, more Demon Boars, got it.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">.</span></li> <li>&quot;Oh, this Zenith has a serious attachment to their Lunar Mate. Introducing the Lunar might be a better hook than kidnapping a random cousin.&quot;</li> </ul><b>Conversely</b>, I've had an ST request &amp; then ignore our past lives - and flat-out invent (horrible) things to demonize us - and I felt <i>zero attachment</i>. It was like being hired for a job and being expected to care about what an ex-employee did in the position. Not my actions, not my problem - I feel neither guilt for their behavior nor pity for their victims.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">And I should note that I have no problem with having prior incarnations who do horrible shit (and I usually include some of that). It's the fact that the ST wanted to super-glue memories that had zero synergy with the character concept that made it foreign and unrelatable.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">If she wanted a &quot;evil 1st Age eugenicist and bio-engineer&quot;, she could have just asked before having us make our characters. <b>But</b> my characters motivation was to close-off a Shadowland in the East. A shaman to a (now dead) tribe (of maybe 30-40 people), how on earth was he to relate to a city, let alone bio-labs, let alone mass eugenics projects? Dude lived in the jungles most of his life hunting and shitting in bushes.</div><hr /><br /> So it's useful if you're an ST requesting past-lives <b>so that</b> you can see the character concept from other angles &amp; see what your players are into.<br /> <br /> But if <b>their</b> past lives are just an excuse for <b>the STs </b>personal fan-fic, I could see most players shrugging and shoving it into their pocket like any other random key or password they encounter while exploring a dungeon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":".  elaborating 08-23-2019, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-25T01:25:13-07:00","id":1332510,"title":"","content":"That does somewhat gel with my experience. The one player in my long-running Solar/Lunar game who was quite interested in their past life, was the player of the PC who was a gentle beauty (rabbit-totem Lunar) who underwent a lot of trauma and lost a lot of friends from the Cult of the Illuminated, and wished that she was instead some sort of badass assassin-warrior. I made her past life a badass giant wolf-monster who partnered up with his Dawn mate for awesome battles. So I think that character saw the past life incarnation as something to strive towards; a model of what she could be.<br /> Whereas most of the rest didn't really have any great link with their current characters, so just, as you said, it got shoved into pockets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-25T21:37:38-07:00","id":1332605,"title":"","content":"For my Chronicle, I used &quot;You all meet in the shattered ruins of the fortress-palace Manse that once belonged to your First Age incarnations, and has haunted your dreams since Exaltation&quot; as the Exalted equivalent to &quot;I dunno, you all meet in an inn&quot;. Because the characters kind of come from all over the place, and I needed them to be a Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7058-kerredai","name":"Kerredai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T00:44:15-07:00","id":1332615,"title":"","content":"It is pretty much a classic. That's how we met in the very first Solar game I ever played.<br /> <br /> Now I am running Lunars, you can just have the PCs invited to a Lunar moot, but with new Solars you have to get a bit deus ex machina, so First Age memories do the trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T00:47:27-07:00","id":1332617,"title":"","content":"Ah, here's another question: with the memories of previous incarnations, do you just use one previous incarnation (I'll assume that of the incarnation at the end of the Age of Dreams) or a whole bunch of different ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T08:18:19-07:00","id":1332652,"title":"","content":"Btw isn\u2019t Lytek supposed to clean the exaltation or whatever to avoid the bleedthrough from previous exaltation like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T08:43:52-07:00","id":1332654,"title":"","content":"In 2nd ed, yes; but not perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T08:56:33-07:00","id":1332657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1332654#post1332654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2nd ed, yes; but not perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s more akin to the memories sometimes not being advantageous, so he removes them; perhaps it would be traumatic, for instance, to have a distinct memory of how your past self died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T12:00:04-07:00","id":1332687,"title":"","content":"Here they've been used largely as markers for story hooks. An oddly grounded deja vu, a password you somehow knew, a familiar name, an unexplained nervousness looking at an altar with shackles...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T09:23:06-07:00","id":1334186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1332028#post1332028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before each session I usually try to write out a couple of pages as a short story that people can read before we play. These stories will flesh out the world in some way. For example, they might show what's going on with important NPC's in the setting, or show how parts of the setting where the PCs are not currently located are changing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, since I'd done plenty of First Age memories, I tried doing this instead. I was a bit worried about spoilers (I nearly put in a big spoiler by accident by putting a bad guy's real name, but I noticed it just before sending out the email). But I think it's been okay.<br /> <br /> I haven't talked to all the players about this, just a few, but they told me they preferred the short stories to the first age dreams. I guess it's more relevant (also, some said that the First Age memories had too much sex in; probably fair!). There was also an interesting difference of opinion about whether it's better to have all the dreams about one particular incarnation (presumably the High First Age incarnation), or lots of different ones. As these characters are Lunars, I had a lot of different incarnations; the point really was to give an overall idea of the various lives they'd had, good and bad, as well as foreshadow some things and very vaguely showcase exalt types that used to exist and no longer do, in case I ever want to do something with that (like Sidereals, Solars, whatever Hearteaters used to be, etc).<br /> But then, I feel if it was all about one previous incarnation, someone particularly important, I'd have wanted to ask them for their previous life's details themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, so I've started writing short stories from NPCs' point of view to send out between sessions. I think it's good for fleshing out the world as you said; it also helps to set the tone of the game, which isn't always easy in game (especially as my setting is Vikings/Anglo-Saxons vs mutant Samurai, but the plot of the first story arc is L'morte D'Arthur crossed with the White Witch; some of the players said they found that a bit odd because they don't really see Arthuria as Viking-esque).<br /> But I think the main thing is it helps the players remember the setting details; names of cultures and places, names of NPCs who've only been mentioned once or twice in-game, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> So this is one I wrote between sessions that had a big fight against two Dragonblood and their soldiers:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Another day of frozen misery. Another day of boredom. </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nandorun Samatsu sighed. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Taizen raised one perfectly-manicured eyebrow. &quot;Well,&quot; said the southerner in his polished accent, &quot;It's your turn.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Samatsu sneered. &quot;Okay!&quot; He turned over one of his tiles, revealing the symbol for Wood.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Taizen gave one of his mocking smiles, and responded immediately, revealing Fire.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Ah! This game is stupid! These tactics would never work in real life!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Taizen gave another mocking half-smile. &quot;Step on a spider, chop up a snake, Nandorun-kun.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">From outside came a cough. &quot;Uh, Taicho-samas?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Samatsu stood up with relief, and threw open the tent's fabric door. Any excuse to get away from Taizen's infernal smirking. How he wished he'd been allowed to go with Jadis, rather than stuck here with that lazy rat!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Report, soldier!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Nandorun-dono!&quot; The guard lazily snapped a sloppy salute. Such undisciplined louts. &quot;There's a hairy barbarian at the gate. His name is Olaf Keelbreaker?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Samatsu frowned. The name wasn't familiar.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;He says we destroyed his village, and killed his family? He's here for revenge?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Taizen gasped. &quot;Nandorun-san!&quot; He grabbed the samurai's shoulder. &quot;That's an Oni!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">At the word oni, the memories all rushed back into Samatsu's head. The memories of that day. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>The city burns. Samatsu weeps as he holds his dead wife in his hands. At his door, the demon laughs, its witch-mark burning on its brow. &quot;You are nothing, little samurai,&quot; it gloats. &quot;I gutted House Nandorun, but I leave you alive. Live in shame, and tell others what happens to those who stand against the Sixty-Six Kuromao, the Black Devil Kings!&quot;</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;An oni!&quot; Samatsu cried. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Twelve years ago, a unit of World Eaters destroyed the village of an oni named Olaf-san,&quot; nodded Taizen. &quot;We thought he'd died, but he lived. Now he's tracked us down.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Samatsu grasped the hilt of his katana, his mouth curving into a cruel smile. &quot;And the fool has come knocking at our front gate.&quot; He marched out, shouting orders. &quot;Ashigaru, form up! Archers, to the wall, but do not loose until I give the order! Spearmen, arms and armour and then to the gate! Boy, my armour!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The boy rushed to clasp Samatsu into his silk-and-scale </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>D\u014d</i></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Taizen frowned, his impassive mask slipping. &quot;Do not let the fires of vengeance consume you, Nandorun-san. This could be a trick.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Samatsu grinned as the boy lifted on his </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>kabuto</i></span></span> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">and attached the </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>menp\u014d</i></span></span> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">face-plate. &quot;You bring Jadis's pet monsters, Tae-san. I will defend the front. Oni are arrogant in their own power, and this fool will get what's coming to him.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ten minutes later, Nandorun Samatsu strode out of the gate onto the snow-covered road, encased in his red armour, the colour of the World Eaters. Behind him crowded spearmen, some in the white-and-blue, others in the red. He felt a coil of fear. What if this was a trick? What if he failed again? But the oni was here. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Those who run only die tired. </i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A motley group stood before him. A hulking brute of a man led them, his face badly scarred, hefting a massive axe with an ivory haft and silver blade. Behind him was a soldier on a huge horse, his eyes in shadow. At his sides were a wild savage encrusted in filth and an older man with bulging, frog-like eyes. Above, a dark bird flew, its beady eyes taking everything in.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;I am Olaf Keelbreaker,&quot; shouted the scarred brute, showing a mouth half-full of smashed teeth. &quot;Twelve years ago, the World-Eaters attacked my village unprovoked and killed my family! I am here to take my revenge!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Samatsu felt his qi surging, red with fiery rage. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>My </i></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">city was attacked by demons like you!&quot; shouted Samatsu. &quot;And today, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>I </i></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">take my revenge!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fast as a hummingbird, Samatsu's katana flew into his hand as he leaped forward. With an animal howl, the ugly monster charged at him... then flew up into the sky screaming, pulled by Jadis's </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>walkuren</i></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For a second, Samatsu felt cheated, but he knew the demon would soon return. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">But, horror of horrors, the oni's two companions began to change. One became a massive gorilla, screaming and beating its chest, while the other transformed into a massive python.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Samatsu's terrified troops hesitantly engaged the two beasts, while he went after the man on the horse.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">His blade flashed with the speed of a crackling fire, but the horsemen parried with supernatural skill. But the man was off-balance, on the defensive. In the corner of his eye, Samatsu saw a woman shooting a massive silver bow, and he heard Taizen shouting to the men who were taking a beating from the beasts, but he was too consumed with rage to care.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Samatsu was about to cut the massive horse's head off, when the horseman cackled. He spoke in a dark and cruel voice. &quot;Foolish Samurai. Don't you remember? It was I who burnt your city, but I did not kill your family. Instead, I cursed them, binding them to me as my animal slaves! Bwahahaha!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For a second, Samatsu paused in horror. It seemed like a lie, but what if it was true? Death was bad enough, but unending slavery to a demon? But then he smiled beneath his mempo. Today, Voharun smiled upon him. Now, he would free his family.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This one I wrote as essentially a session synopsis between games, to help players remember the plot as the next game was a month later:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:10px\">All PCs</span></u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Kari poked the fire, watching the cooking fish. She'd never been a good cook, but a shield-maiden didn't have to be.<br /> &quot;This is bad business, bad business,&quot; growled her father. Karl Kingsmilk had once been a great warrior, if not as great as he liked to boast. Now in his 50s, he should have been at home with his grandkids. &quot;What's my milk-brother going to do?&quot;<br /> Sigurd the Berzerker looked bored. &quot;Well there's a meeting this afternoon, he'll tell us then.&quot;<br /> &quot;I heard that the Lady Amira and Atal the witch have arranged a duel to resolve it,&quot; said Black Paladin in his strange, southern accent.<br /> &quot;A holmgang?&quot; Carl's eyes lit up. He'd rescued Kari's mother from her first husband by killing him in holmgang.<br /> &quot;It was Arcturus who banned holmgang,&quot; said Kari, &quot;He won't want that. It'll be a judicial duel.&quot;<br /> &quot;Who's going to take on Many Spears though?&quot; asked Sigurd.<br /> &quot;The king asked Krove, that beastman, but he refused. I heard he asked Olaf Keelbreaker too, but Olaf hasn't decided,&quot; replied Black Paladin. Kari had thought him some form of black-skinned demon when she'd first seen him, but he was an honourable and thoughtful man.<br /> &quot;I should do it, not some foreigner.&quot; They looked up to find Jarl Galchmei standing above their fire, his face glowering with anger. &quot;It was my brothers who discovered the crime, and my brothers who Many Spears killed escaping.&quot;<br /> Karl looked uneasy. &quot;Look, Galchmei, you yourself told your brothers to leave it. And Many Spears has been one of your best friends for years.&quot;<br /> &quot;Blood comes first,&quot; snarled Galchmei.<br /> Black Paladin frowned. Like Galchmei, he'd also been close to Many Spears.<br /> &quot;Is a duel a good idea? The goddess watches over Many Spears.&quot;<br /> &quot;Fuck the goddess,&quot; snarled Galchmei, never one for reverence.<br /> &quot;Hey,&quot; said Kari, eager to change the conversation. &quot;What's that?&quot; She pointed out north-west. It was snowing, but a set of black shapes were just visible. Mostly man-sized, but some were much, much larger.<br /> &quot;That must be Jarl Olaf of the Mammoth Clan, said Black Paladin. &quot;He was supposed to get here soon. And he's supposed to have Jarl Ragna Half-Rat of Clan Relic with him.&quot;<br /> Karl looked worried. &quot;Ragna is Many Spears' second-cousin. She is going to be awkward.&quot;<br /> &quot;No-one's going to get in the way of my vengeance,&quot; growled Galchmei. The others looked at each other uneasily.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This one I wrote essentially as another synopsis, for a player who missed the session. It also mentions a few details that foreshadow later things; stuff I want players to know, but without drawing attention to. Chekov's guns:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <u>Arcturus</u><br /> It'd been a week and a half of trudging along the snowy road and Alfhild was bored. When the messenger to raise the Fyrd she'd been delighted. She'd taken up her father's spear, Goblin-Woe, and taken her place amongst the warriors. One of the Thanes of Clan Relic had rebelled, and it was time to show the treacherous beastmen their place. But being a soldier was less glamorous than she'd expected; no glorious battle, just a lot of marching. Ivan Lionfriend led the column, so she'd seen a tame lion. But all the other famous heroes had gone ahead on horseback, and she was stuck walking here with the annoying boys from her village.<br /> The weather was miserable. It was Rising Wood, she should be in the fields planting, but it was still snowing. The road was exposed to the angry sea to the south. Also, her dad's wooden shield was too big for her. And she'd heard a rumour that the Thane they were going to fight was Many Spears, the great hero, who'd kidnapped the Queen. But that didn't make sense! Why would he kidnap the Queen? Some of the guys had even said the Queen had run off with Many Spears because the king was impotent, but that sounded like bullshit.<br /> She was broken from her reverie by a cawing sound. A bird flew down near the column. But then it somehow shifted, she blinked, and there stood one of the best looking men she'd ever seen. He wore mail of iron links, a thick golden torc and armrings, and on his head was a steel helmet. Things a farmer's daughter like Alfhild could never afford. She knew without a doubt that this must be Arcturus; Mighty-in-War the skalds called him, Bane-of-Elves, Moon-Loved, Witch-Born, Bull-Hearted, Silver-Tongue, King.<br /> &quot;Column halt!&quot; Arcturus's voice boomed out like an avalanche; as the soldiers stopped all down the column, Alfhild realised all 500 had heard him clearly.<br /> &quot;We are betrayed!&quot; he continued, stern-faced. &quot;The Guild of Merchants has brought in mercenaries, the World Eaters, and seized Caer Moroth!&quot;<br /> Alfhild was shocked. Did that mean Arcturus had been out-manoevured?<br /> &quot;Fear not, my loyal subjects!&quot; As his charming voice settled in her ears, Alfhild forgot what she was thinking about before. Under the glorious King all their enemies would bleed!<br /> &quot;The foeman is mighty. But we are mightier still! Their treachery will only make our own victory more glorious!&quot; As he spoke, Alfhild's mind leaped ahead. She'd kill ten foeman, be named a thane, and return home laden with treasure. Then Bjorn Fair-Face would dump that slut Helga and marry her instead. All around her the Fyrd cheered.<br /> She saw Ivan Lionfriend hurry forward, followed by his lion, and speak to Arcturus quietly. Arcturus lowered his voice, but she just caught it as she was close. &quot;I'd just finished naming new Thanes,&quot; said the King, &quot;Olaf Keelbreaker, Amira and Jin. But then the shaman Atal told me Tabun had appeared to him as a ghost, and said the castle had fallen.&quot;<br /> Ivan looked shocked. &quot;Tabun is dead?&quot;<br /> Atal nodded, grim-faced. &quot;And probably Torsten and Soldva, who I left to guard Caer Moroth.&quot; He gestured to the troops, who were clumsily turning around. &quot;But we've got a large force here, and the Huscarls are riding hard to meet us. And I have the blessing of the Moon God.&quot;<br /> &quot;What of the Queen?&quot; asked Ivan.<br /> Arcturus shook his head. &quot;We'll have to deal with it later. The capital comes first.&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I used to write straightforward session synopses (the PCs did this, then this, then this) but I think this is more interesting. Might be a bit difficult to follow compared to the more straightforward ones though.<br /> <br /> And these two are the last synopses, from the same session (but I was stressed with work and wanted to write more, essentially). The point is to show where the PCs currently are and what's going on, especially as the party has split so they may have not been paying attention and missed what the other group is doing:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <u>Atal, Underfoot and Krove</u><br /> Mighty Pelt was a sad bear. He was on a wooden iceberg, stuck to a big tree with a big white leaf. Humans and Bad Cat kept coming and shouting at him. He tried eating Bad Cat, but it hit him. One human looked nice, but also smelled like dead bear. Sometimes the humans fought for territory. And there was a storm.<br /> Baalu said if Mighty Pelt just waited and didn't fight, the humans would bring him fish. Strange. But he was stuck on a strong branch, and couldn't fight.<br /> The wooden iceberg floated near some land. Mighty Pelt tried to get off the iceberg, but he was still stuck to the tree by a strong branch.<br /> He slept. He woke up. A human was sneaking around. He got up. The branch had come off the tree! He dived into the water, and paddled across to the land. He still had the heavy branch stuck to him, but he was free. He found some woods, and settled down for a nice sleep.<br /> He woke up. In front of him was a human-cave-tree. What? How did that get there? He could see inside Baloo and his son, snug and out of the snow, and one of the other humans, the loud one that smelled like a toad.<br /> He felt something warm and furry resting at his side. A lady-bear? No, it was Bad Cat. Bad Cat had followed him to punch him again! No escape!<br /> <br /> <u>Jin and Olaf</u><br /> Einar Hairy-Arms was in a good mood. His pockets were full of gold, his belly was full, and while the weather was miserable he was in a nice warm dwarf-built keep. He leaned back on his cheer, and raised his full tankard of mead. &quot;To Grim the Rich!&quot;<br /> His friends grinned and raised their own tankards, giving their own toasts. &quot;To Katsunaga the Southman!&quot;, &quot;To the girls of Clan Dragon-Bull!&quot;, &quot;To the Guild of Merchants!&quot;, &quot;To the ales of Caer Moroth!&quot;, &quot;To the White Witch!&quot;, &quot;To the blood of the foeman on our blades!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey,&quot; said Dag Dogbiter. &quot;There's Akiko. We should invite her over.&quot; He waved at the mutant mercenary, while Einar gave a smirk to the others. Dag had been mooning over the mutant since he saw her skewer two guards on one spear.<br /> &quot;Dag!&quot; said Akiko as she swaggered over and sat down, surprisingly graceful in her heavy steel armour. She took Dag's offered mead-horn in her seven-fingered hand. &quot;I see today strange thing, you tell. Is big fat animal, like grey dog, lives in sea. What is?&quot;<br /> Dag thought for a bit. He wasn't the sharpest axe in the woodshed. &quot;Seal?&quot; The others nodded.<br /> &quot;What kind of animals live on your southern beaches then?&quot; asked Magna Axewife.<br /> Akiko paused, pain in her eyes. &quot;Once, crab, fishes, too much birds. Now, nothing. The <i>Kuromao</i> killed all.&quot;<br /> Dag looked awkward. He wanted to flirt, not remind Akiko about her dead family. And they hadn't had been happy when Katsunaga desecrated the Moon-Lord's temple, something they'd rather forget. But Dag was saved by a thrall's interruption. &quot;Uh, Karls? There's something going on outside.&quot;<br /> Einar put his tankard down and stretched. &quot;Come on then.&quot;<br /> The group trooped out into the yard. At the gate, they could see a merchant with a massive black horse arguing with the guards, his eyes in shadow despite the light. He had a huge ugly guard with a mutilated face. The guard stepped forward, pulling the cloth of his huge axe; a massive thing with an ivory haft and a silver blade.<br /> Einar and his mates stepped forward, hefting their axes, but Akiki hissed. \u201cIs <i>Aku-ma</i>, moon demon!\u201d The guy didn't look like a demon, he just looked butt-ugly.<br /> <i>Slice.</i><br /> Einar blinked. The gate guards both slumped to the floor, decapitated in a single stroke. A bloody head rolled out into the yard. The ugly brute stepped through the gate into the yard, hefting his axe like it weighed nothing, followed by the merchant who'd drawn some weird-looking thin sword. Voharun's balls. Einar did not want to die today.<br /> \u201cKatsunaga!\u201d Einar yelled at the thralls. \u201cGet Captain Katsunaga here now or we're fucked!\u201d They ran.<br /> Einar turned back to face the demon. Shit.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-06-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-06T18:31:50-07:00","id":1334276,"title":"","content":"Were you riffing off Olaf Axlebreaker, a pothole in a Far Side cartoon ages ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-07T00:25:37-07:00","id":1334310,"title":"","content":"Huh, I'll have to ask the player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T11:07:17-07:00","id":1334495,"title":"","content":"My last character actually had a quirk with his exaltation such that his mind overrode the body of the recipient of his exaltation, so this was a huge part of his story as he sought to 'get the gang back together' so to speak and gather his old allies (Similarly blessed with their minds passed down their exaltations as well) and reforge some semblance of the First Age in the modern era. This was quite the fun challenge, RP-wise as my character was almost always in full plate and I didn't even know their sex until three sessions in when I rolled on a dice for it. Up till then, I was playing him as a gruff war veteran who even took another PC Solar under his wing as he taught him swordcraft and regaled him with tales of wars long gone. Then I rolled, and my character became a teenage girl from An-Teng (A collaboration of ideas between my ST and myself). I continued as I had, but it led to some hilarity as Valentinian XIII was many, many times not taken seriously because of his youth and slight frame.<br /> <br /> Apart from that, I find past lives or some correlation to them to be an easy framing device for how my characters acquires their artifacts, so I often do have some level of interaction with them. It's just an additional cool piece of flavor for a character, too, and I'm a sucker for stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T04:04:12-07:00","id":1334603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1334495#post1334495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from that, I find past lives or some correlation to them to be an easy framing device for how my characters acquires their artifacts</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly a popular one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T19:08:42-07:00","id":1334751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1334603#post1334603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's certainly a popular one.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I can understand why. The way I keep it 'fresh' is to get an understanding of what I want out of the character and build both the artifact and the past life as aspects of that overall metacharacter. Perhaps the past life was prone to overzealousness? Then their current life will overcorrect, leading to new problems, and their weapon will gain benefits if my character acts in a balanced way? That sort of thing. <br /> <br /> Also, and this is totally a subjective personal opinion, I'm not a huge fan of crafting in general, so this is perhaps the best way of getting these rare magical weapons and armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T03:01:50-07:00","id":1334784,"title":"","content":"I want to like crafting... but compared to the background dots it costs to get artefacts, it's always ended up feeling way too expensive. Maybe if you made artefact weapons and armour for the entire group, but some people don't want it, some people already have them, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I keep it 'fresh' is to get an understanding of what I want out of the character and build both the artifact and the past life as aspects of that overall metacharacter. Perhaps the past life was prone to overzealousness? Then their current life will overcorrect, leading to new problems, and their weapon will gain benefits if my character acts in a balanced way? That sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T16:17:41-07:00","id":1334995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1332015-do-you-use-memories-of-previous-exaltations-in-your-chronicles-how?p=1334784#post1334784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to like crafting... but compared to the background dots it costs to get artefacts, it's always ended up feeling way too expensive. Maybe if you made artefact weapons and armour for the entire group, but some people don't want it, some people already have them, etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish we had some sort of story beat system that would handle things like this. A bit like how you can introduce facts with Lore. But rather, with Artifacts, each Evocation would specifically introduce some bit of history, story hook, location, past life, or some such Chronicle-interactive detail. I do somewhat miss older systems' point-buy schemes for such things, even.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T04:55:02-07:00","id":1343381,"title":"","content":"I have several moments where my solar has a storyline where she begins to dream of her past life<br /> <br /> The first part is when the sun expands to cover the entire sky, when she was a medic healing her tribe of illness. As the moon rose to shield the sun from that terrible heat, she began to draw the second breathe...<br /> <br /> The second is when she watches a woman, a girl, with contempt, until she throws a cloud of obsidian butterflies. And then contempt turns to curiosity, and then wonder, and then discovery<br /> <br /> The third, is when she sits amongst a great gathering. And then something goes wrong. People begin choking. She rushes over, to heal her friends. And then, something explodes, and a great cloud of smoke covers her vision. As she runs out of the dining hall, she sees an army of her loyal friends and companions. Firing upon her. Dodging for her life and confused, she searches for the exit or a way to escpe. And then she trips. And as she lays down there, nursing her now broken ankle, she watches the glowing beams of light fall from the sky onto her...<br /> <br /> This is for her to see the Usurpation, listen and act as a tutoring for High Realm, and for her to discover sorcery. <br /> <br /> Another thing is when she starts talking about this on TV, and the other show hosts are torn on it either being bullshit people spew like how everyone is a king or a general or cleopetra, or something to it, because hey, this is the only person on the planet with superpowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T14:59:52-07:00","id":1344076,"title":"","content":"It depends on the group. My experience with these is that i added them for flavor in the game to build RPing. One PC had memories of finding a baby-behemoth and making friends with him. It grew one meter every year. 5000 years later this Behemoth's idea of &quot;playtime&quot; was decidedly more destructive than when it was small.<br /> <br /> Another pair of PCs were GF/BF in real life and RPed (tastefully) an in character romance. I... subverted that a little bit with their first age memories of how screwed up things got. They liked it quite a bit.<br /> <br /> For the sorceror, I gave them memories of the Time Before, when the primordials were free.<br /> <br /> It was fun, added some flavor, gave them something to think about. The big thing was that I had no expectations of how it would get used. It was something I did for fun and enrichment of the game, and let the players choose how to use or not use the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}